This is for springboot test or java test.
Just Copy the template folder can create a springboot project for test.
Also simple java code can write anywhere, but also write in 'simple' folder.

add a filter:
1. add XXXFilter.java implements Filter 
2. overwrite doFilter and add @WebFilter in XXXFilter.java
3. add @ServletComponantScan in XXXApplication.java

add an interceptor:
1. add XXXInterceptor.java implements HandlerInterceptor
2. overwrite preHandle/postHandle/afterComplete 
3. add InterceptorConfig.java implements WebMvcConfigurer and overwrite addInterceptors and add @configuration

add a custom starter:(with this, you should know how spring boot work with starter)
1. implement your functional class, like FunA.java (no need @component)
2. add autoconfigure class FunAConfiguration,  use @bean to new the FunA class.
3. add file resources/META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports 
(in 2.7 name resources/META-INF/spring.factories, no use any more) to add the class 1'com.xx.xx.FunAConfiguration'
4. maven clean and maven install
5. if need, can add a config class to use @configurationproperity or @value, this config call need @component.   And also can make the functionaal call as a filter/interceptor, like spring security
6. conditon control under @configuration or @bean in FunAconfiguration.clall.  like 
@CondtionalOn[Property|Class|MissingClass|MissingBean|Resource|WebApplication], others all simeple.
@CondtionalOnProperty(prefix="", name="", havingValue="", mathIfMissing=false)
 
use spring execption:
1. use @ExecptionHandler(xxx.class) (any special execption class or Execption.call for all other) for a method within any controller,  but only affect iner the controller.
2. use @ControllerAdvise or @restcontrollerAdvise for a class,  then with the class, use @ExceptionHandler(xxx.class) for any mothods.    this is global execption handler.
3. generally within any method, we return a map with Map<String, object>